# These images COPY/ADD nothing — they only install packages from the network.
# The build context is therefore intentionally empty: exclude everything, so no
# repo file (agent/IDE config, git history, docs, credentials) can ever be sent
# to the Docker daemon or leak into a layer.
#
# The Dockerfile named by `docker build -f` is read separately and is unaffected.
# If a future change needs a file in the image, whitelist it explicitly, e.g.:
#   !entrypoint.sh
*
